exports[`investecAdapter.normalize — snapshots > normalizes 13385 1`] = `
{
  "applyUrl": "https://careers.investec.co.za/jobs/vacancy/relationship-manager--business-and-commercial-banking-13385-cape-town/13403/description/",
  "brand": "Investec",
  "category": "Sales",
  "country": "ZA",
  "descriptionHtml": "<p>Description of the role </p>
<p>The Relationship Manager is accountable for the end‑to‑end management of client relationships within an allocated portfolio. The role is focused on protecting and growing the existing book, deepening client engagement, driving utilisation of products, and increasing Investec Business and Commercial Banking's market share and top‑line revenue.<br />The Relationship Manager is responsible for building deep, profitable, and sustainable client relationships through proactive portfolio management, structured product entrenchment, and the identification and execution of cross‑sell opportunities across Business and Commercial Banking (BCB) and the broader Investec Group.</p>
<p>Key Deliverables</p>
<p>•    Retention, defence, and growth of existing facilities within the allocated client portfolio.<br />•    Entrenchment of clients across BCB and the broader Investec Group, increasing overall wallet share.<br />•    Successful implementation, entrenchment, and optimisation of core banking products, including:<br />o    Trade and Import Finance<br />o    Transactional Banking and Overdrafts<br />o    Borrowing Base Facilities<br />o    Term Lending<br />o    Asset Finance<br />•    Identification and execution of cross‑sell and upsell opportunities to deepen client relationships and enhance profitability.<br />•    Growth in operating income through improved utilisation and effective product mix optimisation.<br />•    Origination of new client opportunities via referrals to the New Business Development team.<br />•    Active participation in the credit process in partnership with Portfolio Consultants, applying strong client insight and commercial judgement.<br />•    Seamless implementation and activation of newly approved or amended credit facilities.<br />•    Delivery of a “Private Banking for your Business” client experience, characterised by high‑touch engagement, responsiveness, and proactive relationship management.</p>
<p>Responsibilities:</p>
<p>Client &amp; Portfolio Management<br />•    Develop a thorough understanding of clients' businesses, industries, and financial drivers.<br />•    Perform as part of a deal team with Portfolio Consultants and ICs to best serve client requirements<br />•    Assess and manage the portfolio to ensure appropriate growth, defence, and entrenchment strategies are applied.<br />•    Proactively engage clients to grow facilities and address causes of low utilisation.<br />•    Ensure optimal product mix to achieve appropriate blended returns.<br />•    Take ownership of post-credit implementation and activation of approved facilities and amendments.<br />Product Entrenchment &amp; Cross-Selling<br />•    Identify opportunities to further entrench clients within BCB and the broader Group.<br />•    Drive cross-sell initiatives across transactional banking, trade finance, borrowing base facilities, debtor finance, asset finance and other relevant solutions.<br />•    Partner with internal product specialists to ensure full client adoption of appropriate banking solutions.<br />•    Increase product penetration and long-term client “stickiness” within the portfolio.<br />Credit &amp; Risk Management<br />•    Participate actively in the credit process as part of the deal team.<br />•    Provide detailed client insights to support sound credit decisions.<br />•    Maintain strong credit oversight and portfolio quality.<br />•    Ensure adherence to internal governance, risk frameworks and regulatory standards.<br />Stakeholder &amp; Operational Management<br />•    Partner closely with Credit, Operations, Legal and other internal stakeholders to deliver seamless client execution.<br />•    Prepare and implement operational requirements for newly activated deals.<br />•    Collaborate across the internal value chain to deliver integrated solutions.</p>
<p>Qualifications, Experience and Skills</p>
<p>•    BCom degree or equivalent financial qualification.<br />•    Minimum of 5 years' relevant experience within Business Banking, supported by a strong lending and credit background.<br />•    FAIS accreditation (required to operate as a licensed representative for intermediary services across long‑ and short‑term deposits) preferred.<br />•    Solid commercial and financial acumen, with proven ability to read and interpret Annual Financial Statements.<br />•    Strong product knowledge across Trade and Import Finance (including forwarding and clearing/logistics), Borrowing Base Facilities, Term Lending, Asset Finance, Transactional Banking and Overdrafts.<br />•    Demonstrated experience managing senior client relationships at MD, FD and CEO level, with the ability to engage effectively with executive stakeholders.<br />•    Proven capability to originate, upsell and cross‑sell tailored banking solutions.<br />•    Well-developed negotiation, problem‑solving, planning and prioritisation skills.<br />•    Strong collaborator with a track record of working effectively across internal teams and multiple stakeholders.</p>
<p>Personal Attributes</p>
<p>•    Dynamic, energetic and driven.<br />•    Demonstrates tenacity, integrity and sound judgement.<br />•    High level of professionalism and client-centric mindset.<br />•    Embraces Investec's culture of out-of-the-ordinary thinking and challenging convention.<br />•    Values diversity, competency and flexible leadership in pursuit of business growth.</p>
<p>What We Value</p>
<p>At Investec we seek creative, talented people with passion, energy and stamina, who collaborate unselfishly.</p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>",
  "descriptionText": "Description of the role The Relationship Manager is accountable for the end‑to‑end management of client relationships within an allocated portfolio. The role is focused on protecting and growing the existing book, deepening client engagement, driving utilisation of products, and increasing Investec Business and Commercial Banking's market share and top‑line revenue. The Relationship Manager is responsible for building deep, profitable, and sustainable client relationships through proactive portfolio management, structured product entrenchment, and the identification and execution of cross‑sell opportunities across Business and Commercial Banking (BCB) and the broader Investec Group. Key Deliverables • Retention, defence, and growth of existing facilities within the allocated client portfolio. • Entrenchment of clients across BCB and the broader Investec Group, increasing overall wallet share. • Successful implementation, entrenchment, and optimisation of core banking products, including: o Trade and Import Finance o Transactional Banking and Overdrafts o Borrowing Base Facilities o Term Lending o Asset Finance • Identification and execution of cross‑sell and upsell opportunities to deepen client relationships and enhance profitability. • Growth in operating income through improved utilisation and effective product mix optimisation. • Origination of new client opportunities via referrals to the New Business Development team. • Active participation in the credit process in partnership with Portfolio Consultants, applying strong client insight and commercial judgement. • Seamless implementation and activation of newly approved or amended credit facilities. • Delivery of a “Private Banking for your Business” client experience, characterised by high‑touch engagement, responsiveness, and proactive relationship management. Responsibilities: Client & Portfolio Management • Develop a thorough understanding of clients' businesses, industries, and financial drivers. • Perform as part of a deal team with Portfolio Consultants and ICs to best serve client requirements • Assess and manage the portfolio to ensure appropriate growth, defence, and entrenchment strategies are applied. • Proactively engage clients to grow facilities and address causes of low utilisation. • Ensure optimal product mix to achieve appropriate blended returns. • Take ownership of post-credit implementation and activation of approved facilities and amendments. Product Entrenchment & Cross-Selling • Identify opportunities to further entrench clients within BCB and the broader Group. • Drive cross-sell initiatives across transactional banking, trade finance, borrowing base facilities, debtor finance, asset finance and other relevant solutions. • Partner with internal product specialists to ensure full client adoption of appropriate banking solutions. • Increase product penetration and long-term client “stickiness” within the portfolio. Credit & Risk Management • Participate actively in the credit process as part of the deal team. • Provide detailed client insights to support sound credit decisions. • Maintain strong credit oversight and portfolio quality. • Ensure adherence to internal governance, risk frameworks and regulatory standards. Stakeholder & Operational Management • Partner closely with Credit, Operations, Legal and other internal stakeholders to deliver seamless client execution. • Prepare and implement operational requirements for newly activated deals. • Collaborate across the internal value chain to deliver integrated solutions. Qualifications, Experience and Skills • BCom degree or equivalent financial qualification. • Minimum of 5 years' relevant experience within Business Banking, supported by a strong lending and credit background. • FAIS accreditation (required to operate as a licensed representative for intermediary services across long‑ and short‑term deposits) preferred. • Solid commercial and financial acumen, with proven ability to read and interpret Annual Financial Statements. • Strong product knowledge across Trade and Import Finance (including forwarding and clearing/logistics), Borrowing Base Facilities, Term Lending, Asset Finance, Transactional Banking and Overdrafts. • Demonstrated experience managing senior client relationships at MD, FD and CEO level, with the ability to engage effectively with executive stakeholders. • Proven capability to originate, upsell and cross‑sell tailored banking solutions. • Well-developed negotiation, problem‑solving, planning and prioritisation skills. • Strong collaborator with a track record of working effectively across internal teams and multiple stakeholders. Personal Attributes • Dynamic, energetic and driven. • Demonstrates tenacity, integrity and sound judgement. • High level of professionalism and client-centric mindset. • Embraces Investec's culture of out-of-the-ordinary thinking and challenging convention. • Values diversity, competency and flexible leadership in pursuit of business growth. What We Value At Investec we seek creative, talented people with passion, energy and stamina, who collaborate unselfishly.",
  "employmentType": "Full-time",
  "excerpt": "Description of the role The Relationship Manager is accountable for the end‑to‑end management of client relationships within an allocated portfolio. The role is focused on protecting and growing the existing book, deepening client engagement, driving utilisation of products, and increasing Investec Business and Commercial Banking's market share and top‑line revenue.",
  "id": "investec:13385",
  "locations": [
    {
      "city": "Cape Town",
      "province": "Western Cape",
      "raw": "Cape Town",
    },
  ],
  "postedDate": null,
  "primaryLocation": "Cape Town, Western Cape",
  "source": "investec",
  "title": "Relationship Manager- Business and Commercial Banking",
}
`;

exports[`investecAdapter.normalize — snapshots > normalizes 13784 1`] = `
{
  "applyUrl": "https://careers.investec.co.za/jobs/vacancy/technical-lead---rewards-13784-sandton/13802/description/",
  "brand": "Investec",
  "category": "Software & IT",
  "country": "ZA",
  "descriptionHtml": "<p>Description</p>
<p>We are looking for a Technical Lead to drive the technical direction, quality, and health of the Investec Rewards technology platform and its supporting engineering systems.<br />This role is suited to an experienced engineer who wants to remain hands-on, while stepping into a broader leadership position. As a Tech Lead, you will spend less time on day-to-day feature delivery and more time solving complex engineering problems, shaping system design, and enabling your team to deliver high-quality, scalable solutions.<br />You will work closely with Engineering Leads, Application Owners, and Architects to ensure systems are well-designed, maintainable, and aligned to our engineering standards. You will also play a key role in mentoring engineers and raising the overall engineering bar within the team.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>Key Responsibilities</p>
<p>•    Own the technical design and architecture of systems within your team, while partnering with Engineering Leads and Architects on key technical decisions<br />•    Maintain the long-term health of systems, addressing risks such as coupling, scalability, and technical debt<br />•    Drive adoption and consistent use of engineering standards and best practices<br />•    Set and uphold a high bar for code quality through active participation in code reviews<br />•    Ensure solutions are maintainable, testable, and production-ready<br />•    Intervene where necessary to address quality issues or engineering gaps<br />•    Support delivery by unblocking teams and resolving complex technical challenges<br />•    Partner with Application Owners to ensure delivery is technically sound and sustainable<br />•    Participate in incident response and lead technical problem-solving when required<br />•    Mentor and coach engineers, particularly Senior Software Engineers<br />•    Provide constructive feedback to support individual and team growth<br />•    Contribute to platform roadmap discussions and technical direction<br />•    Monitor and optimise cloud usage, balancing cost, performance, and reliability<br />•    Participate in engineering forums, communities of practice, and knowledge sharing<br />•    Contribute to broader engineering initiatives, standards, and reusable components</p>
<p> </p>
<p>Qualifications, Experience and Skills</p>
<p>•    Technical Leadership: Experience defining technical direction, establishing engineering standards, conducting architecture, design and code reviews, and mentoring engineers across complex technology platforms.<br />•    Proficient in Programming Languages and Frameworks: Strong hands-on experience with .NET, C#, TypeScript and modern software engineering practices, with the ability to guide teams in designing and delivering scalable, maintainable and resilient solutions.<br />•    Front-end Development: Strong knowledge of Angular, TypeScript, HTML and CSS, with experience delivering modern customer-facing web applications and guiding front-end engineering standards.<br />•    Back-end Development and Solution Architecture: Experience designing distributed systems, APIs and enterprise applications, with the ability to make sound architectural decisions that balance business needs, engineering quality and long-term platform sustainability.<br />•    Cloud Engineering: Strong Microsoft Azure experience, including cloud-native services, containerised workloads, security, monitoring, infrastructure automation and cost optimisation.<br />•    Databases and Data Management: Experience working with SQL, relational databases, data integration patterns and performance optimisation across enterprise platforms.<br />•    API Development and Integration: Ability to design, govern and support integrations across internal and external systems using modern API and service-oriented architecture principles.<br />•    Version Control and Engineering Governance: Experience with Git, pull request processes, source control governance and the implementation of engineering standards and best practices across teams.<br />•    DevOps and Continuous Delivery: Strong understanding of Azure DevOps, CI/CD pipelines, release management, infrastructure automation and modern software delivery practices.<br />•    Engineering Quality and Operational Excellence: Experience driving code quality, testing standards, incident management, root cause analysis and continuous improvement to ensure solutions are production-ready and operationally resilient.<br />•    Technical Stewardship: Experience maintaining the long-term health of systems by driving engineering quality, managing technical debt, improving resilience, and ensuring solutions remain scalable, maintainable and aligned to architectural standards.<br />•    Security Best Practices: Strong understanding of secure software development, authentication, authorisation and vulnerability management within regulated environments.<br />•    Stakeholder Management and Communication: Excellent communication skills with the ability to engage engineers, architects, product owners, business stakeholders and senior leadership while influencing technical outcomes.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>Investec Culture </p>
<p>At Investec we look for intelligent, energetic people filled with passion, integrity and curiosity. We value individuals who in turn value our culture that is, a flexible attitude comfortable to live with ambiguity and willing to challenge the status quo. Diversity, talent and leadership are respected in pursuit of the growth of our business. People who can manage themselves and build strong relationships in order to get things done, will perform in out of the ordinary ways in our environment. </p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>",
  "descriptionText": "Description We are looking for a Technical Lead to drive the technical direction, quality, and health of the Investec Rewards technology platform and its supporting engineering systems. This role is suited to an experienced engineer who wants to remain hands-on, while stepping into a broader leadership position. As a Tech Lead, you will spend less time on day-to-day feature delivery and more time solving complex engineering problems, shaping system design, and enabling your team to deliver high-quality, scalable solutions. You will work closely with Engineering Leads, Application Owners, and Architects to ensure systems are well-designed, maintainable, and aligned to our engineering standards. You will also play a key role in mentoring engineers and raising the overall engineering bar within the team. Key Responsibilities • Own the technical design and architecture of systems within your team, while partnering with Engineering Leads and Architects on key technical decisions • Maintain the long-term health of systems, addressing risks such as coupling, scalability, and technical debt • Drive adoption and consistent use of engineering standards and best practices • Set and uphold a high bar for code quality through active participation in code reviews • Ensure solutions are maintainable, testable, and production-ready • Intervene where necessary to address quality issues or engineering gaps • Support delivery by unblocking teams and resolving complex technical challenges • Partner with Application Owners to ensure delivery is technically sound and sustainable • Participate in incident response and lead technical problem-solving when required • Mentor and coach engineers, particularly Senior Software Engineers • Provide constructive feedback to support individual and team growth • Contribute to platform roadmap discussions and technical direction • Monitor and optimise cloud usage, balancing cost, performance, and reliability • Participate in engineering forums, communities of practice, and knowledge sharing • Contribute to broader engineering initiatives, standards, and reusable components Qualifications, Experience and Skills • Technical Leadership: Experience defining technical direction, establishing engineering standards, conducting architecture, design and code reviews, and mentoring engineers across complex technology platforms. • Proficient in Programming Languages and Frameworks: Strong hands-on experience with .NET, C#, TypeScript and modern software engineering practices, with the ability to guide teams in designing and delivering scalable, maintainable and resilient solutions. • Front-end Development: Strong knowledge of Angular, TypeScript, HTML and CSS, with experience delivering modern customer-facing web applications and guiding front-end engineering standards. • Back-end Development and Solution Architecture: Experience designing distributed systems, APIs and enterprise applications, with the ability to make sound architectural decisions that balance business needs, engineering quality and long-term platform sustainability. • Cloud Engineering: Strong Microsoft Azure experience, including cloud-native services, containerised workloads, security, monitoring, infrastructure automation and cost optimisation. • Databases and Data Management: Experience working with SQL, relational databases, data integration patterns and performance optimisation across enterprise platforms. • API Development and Integration: Ability to design, govern and support integrations across internal and external systems using modern API and service-oriented architecture principles. • Version Control and Engineering Governance: Experience with Git, pull request processes, source control governance and the implementation of engineering standards and best practices across teams. • DevOps and Continuous Delivery: Strong understanding of Azure DevOps, CI/CD pipelines, release management, infrastructure automation and modern software delivery practices. • Engineering Quality and Operational Excellence: Experience driving code quality, testing standards, incident management, root cause analysis and continuous improvement to ensure solutions are production-ready and operationally resilient. • Technical Stewardship: Experience maintaining the long-term health of systems by driving engineering quality, managing technical debt, improving resilience, and ensuring solutions remain scalable, maintainable and aligned to architectural standards. • Security Best Practices: Strong understanding of secure software development, authentication, authorisation and vulnerability management within regulated environments. • Stakeholder Management and Communication: Excellent communication skills with the ability to engage engineers, architects, product owners, business stakeholders and senior leadership while influencing technical outcomes. Investec Culture At Investec we look for intelligent, energetic people filled with passion, integrity and curiosity. We value individuals who in turn value our culture that is, a flexible attitude comfortable to live with ambiguity and willing to challenge the status quo. Diversity, talent and leadership are respected in pursuit of the growth of our business. People who can manage themselves and build strong relationships in order to get things done, will perform in out of the ordinary ways in our environment.",
  "employmentType": "Full-time",
  "excerpt": "Description We are looking for a Technical Lead to drive the technical direction, quality, and health of the Investec Rewards technology platform and its supporting engineering systems. This role is suited to an experienced engineer who wants to remain hands-on, while stepping into a broader leadership position.",
  "id": "investec:13784",
  "locations": [],
  "postedDate": null,
  "primaryLocation": null,
  "source": "investec",
  "title": "Technical Lead - Rewards",
}
`;

exports[`investecAdapter.normalize — snapshots > normalizes 13804 1`] = `
{
  "applyUrl": "https://careers.investec.co.za/jobs/vacancy/mobile-app-developer--13804-sandton/13822/description/",
  "brand": "Investec",
  "category": "Software & IT",
  "country": "ZA",
  "descriptionHtml": "<p>Description</p>
<p>The Mobile Developer for Investec Business Online (IBOL) forms part of the Investec Business &amp; Commercial Banking (BCB) division and operates within the BCB IT environment.</p>
<p>This is a hands-on engineering role focused on building, maintaining, securing, and supporting enterprise-grade mobile applications across iOS and Android using React Native, Expo, TypeScript, and modern mobile delivery tooling.</p>
<p>The role contributes to reliable mobile delivery by translating business and design requirements into high-quality technical solutions, integrating with enterprise services, supporting CI/CD and release processes, and maintaining strong engineering discipline across code quality, testing, security, performance, accessibility, and production support.</p>
<p>The Mobile Developer works closely with product owners, designers, QA, backend engineers, platform teams, architecture, and operations to deliver secure, scalable, maintainable, and customer-focused mobile outcomes aligned with Investec BCB priorities</p>
<p>Key Responsibilities</p>
<p>Mobile Engineering Delivery &amp; Execution</p>
<ul>
<li>Build, enhance, and maintain mobile application features across iOS and Android using React Native, Expo, TypeScript, JavaScript, and React fundamentals.</li>
<li>Translate business requirements, wireframes, Figma designs, and design-system guidance into polished, accessible, and maintainable mobile user interfaces.</li>
<li>Contribute to end-to-end delivery from refinement and development through testing, deployment, release, and post-implementation support.</li>
<li>Apply sound engineering judgement when using AI-assisted development tools such as Codex, Cursor, Copilot, or ChatGPT to improve productivity without compromising accountability or quality.</li>
</ul>
<p>Enterprise Mobile Tooling, Monorepos &amp; Shared Packages</p>
<ul>
<li>Work effectively within mobile monorepos, shared packages, dependency management models, and workspace tooling.</li>
<li>Support sustainable mobile architecture by keeping shared components, packages, and platform conventions clean, reusable, and well documented.</li>
</ul>
<p>CI/CD, Build, Signing &amp; Release Management</p>
<ul>
<li>Support Azure DevOps CI/CD using YAML pipelines, secure files and secrets, automated builds, automated testing, code-signing, and release approvals.</li>
<li>Build, sign, distribute, and support mobile applications through App Store Connect, TestFlight, Google Play Console, and approved internal distribution channels.</li>
<li>Contribute to reliable release processes, versioning discipline, environment readiness, and release evidence required for enterprise governance.</li>
</ul>
<p>Integration, Security &amp; Enterprise Services</p>
<ul>
<li>Integrate mobile applications with RESTful APIs, authentication flows, secure storage, and enterprise backend services.</li>
<li>Apply good mobile security practices, data privacy awareness, and secure coding principles in line with banking and internal governance expectations.</li>
<li>Identify and escalate technical risks, integration constraints, security considerations, and operational dependencies early.</li>
</ul>
<p>Quality Engineering, Observability &amp; Production Support</p>
<ul>
<li>Contribute to automated testing, TDD/BDD practices, mobile quality gates, code review, and defect prevention.</li>
<li>Improve mobile performance, accessibility, observability, maintainability, and resilience across production applications.</li>
<li>Support production incidents, diagnostics, root-cause analysis, and continuous improvement of mobile reliability.</li>
</ul>
<p>Agile Collaboration &amp; Engineering Discipline</p>
<ul>
<li>Work within Agile/Scrum delivery practices, contributing to sprint planning, backlog refinement, reviews, retrospectives, and transparent progress tracking in Azure DevOps.</li>
<li>Demonstrate strong Git discipline, clear pull requests, constructive code reviews, and accountability for the quality of software shipped.</li>
</ul>
<p>• Collaborate effectively with product, design, QA, backend, platform, architecture, and operations stakeholders.</p>
<p>Qualifications, Experience and Skills</p>
<p>ESSENTIAL TECHNICAL KNOWLEDGE</p>
<ul>
<li>Strong React Native, Expo ecosystem, and TypeScript experience.</li>
<li>Strong JavaScript and React fundamentals, including modern state management and navigation patterns.</li>
<li>Experience building and maintaining iOS and Android apps in enterprise environments.</li>
<li>Experience using error and analytics tools like Dynatrace/Sentry/Splunk.</li>
<li>Strong understanding of monorepos, shared packages, dependency management, and mobile workspace tooling.</li>
<li>Experience with Azure DevOps CI/CD, including YAML pipelines, secure files/secrets, automated builds, testing, signing, and release approvals.</li>
<li>Practical experience building, signing, distributing, and supporting mobile apps through App Store Connect, TestFlight, Google Play Console, and internal distribution channels.</li>
<li>Experience integrating with RESTful APIs, authentication flows, secure storage, and enterprise backend services.</li>
<li>Good understanding of mobile security, performance, accessibility, observability, and production support.</li>
<li>Experience with automated testing, TDD/BDD practices, and mobile quality gates.</li>
<li>Ability to implement polished UI from Figma, wireframes, and design systems.</li>
<li>Strong Git, code review, Agile/Scrum, and engineering delivery discipline.</li>
<li>Comfortable using AI-assisted development tools such as Codex, Cursor, Copilot, or ChatGPT to improve productivity while maintaining accountability, code quality, and sound engineering judgement.</li>
</ul>
<p>DESIRABLE SKILLS</p>
<ul>
<li>Native iOS/Android experience with Swift/Kotlin or native module development is advantageous.</li>
<li>Azure certifications such as AZ-900, AZ-204, or AZ-400 are advantageous.</li>
<li>Experience in Digital / Online Banking channels and platforms is advantageous.</li>
<li>Understanding of payments, foreign exchange, lending, and other transactional banking products is advantageous.</li>
</ul>
<p>SUMMARY PROFILE</p>
<p>We are looking for a modern mobile engineer who can work confidently across React Native, Expo, TypeScript, enterprise CI/CD, mobile distribution, and production support. The ideal candidate uses AI tools intelligently to accelerate delivery, but still demonstrates strong fundamentals, ownership, security awareness, and accountability for the software they ship.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>Investec Culture </p>
<p>At Investec we look for intelligent, energetic people filled with passion, integrity and curiosity. We value individuals who in turn value our culture that is, a flexible attitude comfortable to live with ambiguity and willing to challenge the status quo. Diversity, talent and leadership are respected in pursuit of the growth of our business. People who can manage themselves and build strong relationships in order to get things done, will perform in out of the ordinary ways in our environment. </p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>",
  "descriptionText": "Description The Mobile Developer for Investec Business Online (IBOL) forms part of the Investec Business & Commercial Banking (BCB) division and operates within the BCB IT environment. This is a hands-on engineering role focused on building, maintaining, securing, and supporting enterprise-grade mobile applications across iOS and Android using React Native, Expo, TypeScript, and modern mobile delivery tooling. The role contributes to reliable mobile delivery by translating business and design requirements into high-quality technical solutions, integrating with enterprise services, supporting CI/CD and release processes, and maintaining strong engineering discipline across code quality, testing, security, performance, accessibility, and production support. The Mobile Developer works closely with product owners, designers, QA, backend engineers, platform teams, architecture, and operations to deliver secure, scalable, maintainable, and customer-focused mobile outcomes aligned with Investec BCB priorities Key Responsibilities Mobile Engineering Delivery & Execution Build, enhance, and maintain mobile application features across iOS and Android using React Native, Expo, TypeScript, JavaScript, and React fundamentals. Translate business requirements, wireframes, Figma designs, and design-system guidance into polished, accessible, and maintainable mobile user interfaces. Contribute to end-to-end delivery from refinement and development through testing, deployment, release, and post-implementation support. Apply sound engineering judgement when using AI-assisted development tools such as Codex, Cursor, Copilot, or ChatGPT to improve productivity without compromising accountability or quality. Enterprise Mobile Tooling, Monorepos & Shared Packages Work effectively within mobile monorepos, shared packages, dependency management models, and workspace tooling. Support sustainable mobile architecture by keeping shared components, packages, and platform conventions clean, reusable, and well documented. CI/CD, Build, Signing & Release Management Support Azure DevOps CI/CD using YAML pipelines, secure files and secrets, automated builds, automated testing, code-signing, and release approvals. Build, sign, distribute, and support mobile applications through App Store Connect, TestFlight, Google Play Console, and approved internal distribution channels. Contribute to reliable release processes, versioning discipline, environment readiness, and release evidence required for enterprise governance. Integration, Security & Enterprise Services Integrate mobile applications with RESTful APIs, authentication flows, secure storage, and enterprise backend services. Apply good mobile security practices, data privacy awareness, and secure coding principles in line with banking and internal governance expectations. Identify and escalate technical risks, integration constraints, security considerations, and operational dependencies early. Quality Engineering, Observability & Production Support Contribute to automated testing, TDD/BDD practices, mobile quality gates, code review, and defect prevention. Improve mobile performance, accessibility, observability, maintainability, and resilience across production applications. Support production incidents, diagnostics, root-cause analysis, and continuous improvement of mobile reliability. Agile Collaboration & Engineering Discipline Work within Agile/Scrum delivery practices, contributing to sprint planning, backlog refinement, reviews, retrospectives, and transparent progress tracking in Azure DevOps. Demonstrate strong Git discipline, clear pull requests, constructive code reviews, and accountability for the quality of software shipped. • Collaborate effectively with product, design, QA, backend, platform, architecture, and operations stakeholders. Qualifications, Experience and Skills ESSENTIAL TECHNICAL KNOWLEDGE Strong React Native, Expo ecosystem, and TypeScript experience. Strong JavaScript and React fundamentals, including modern state management and navigation patterns. Experience building and maintaining iOS and Android apps in enterprise environments. Experience using error and analytics tools like Dynatrace/Sentry/Splunk. Strong understanding of monorepos, shared packages, dependency management, and mobile workspace tooling. Experience with Azure DevOps CI/CD, including YAML pipelines, secure files/secrets, automated builds, testing, signing, and release approvals. Practical experience building, signing, distributing, and supporting mobile apps through App Store Connect, TestFlight, Google Play Console, and internal distribution channels. Experience integrating with RESTful APIs, authentication flows, secure storage, and enterprise backend services. Good understanding of mobile security, performance, accessibility, observability, and production support. Experience with automated testing, TDD/BDD practices, and mobile quality gates. Ability to implement polished UI from Figma, wireframes, and design systems. Strong Git, code review, Agile/Scrum, and engineering delivery discipline. Comfortable using AI-assisted development tools such as Codex, Cursor, Copilot, or ChatGPT to improve productivity while maintaining accountability, code quality, and sound engineering judgement. DESIRABLE SKILLS Native iOS/Android experience with Swift/Kotlin or native module development is advantageous. Azure certifications such as AZ-900, AZ-204, or AZ-400 are advantageous. Experience in Digital / Online Banking channels and platforms is advantageous. Understanding of payments, foreign exchange, lending, and other transactional banking products is advantageous. SUMMARY PROFILE We are looking for a modern mobile engineer who can work confidently across React Native, Expo, TypeScript, enterprise CI/CD, mobile distribution, and production support. The ideal candidate uses AI tools intelligently to accelerate delivery, but still demonstrates strong fundamentals, ownership, security awareness, and accountability for the software they ship. Investec Culture At Investec we look for intelligent, energetic people filled with passion, integrity and curiosity. We value individuals who in turn value our culture that is, a flexible attitude comfortable to live with ambiguity and willing to challenge the status quo. Diversity, talent and leadership are respected in pursuit of the growth of our business. People who can manage themselves and build strong relationships in order to get things done, will perform in out of the ordinary ways in our environment.",
  "employmentType": "Full-time",
  "excerpt": "Description The Mobile Developer for Investec Business Online (IBOL) forms part of the Investec Business & Commercial Banking (BCB) division and operates within the BCB IT environment. This is a hands-on engineering role focused on building, maintaining, securing, and supporting enterprise-grade mobile applications across iOS and Android using React Native, Expo, TypeScript, and modern mobile…",
